==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|ru|cu|побѣдити}}, from {{der|ru|sla-pro|*poběditi}}, from {{m|sla-pro|*běditi}}. Related to the noun {{m|ru|беда́}}. Compare {{cog|sh|побије́дити}}/{{m|sh|pobijéditi}}, {{cog|bg|победя́}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|победи́ть}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-победить.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|победи́ть|pf|impf=побежда́ть|vn=побе́да<q:nomen resultatis>,победи́тель<q:nomen agentis>}}

# to [[win]], to be [[victorious]] over, to [[conquer]], to [[vanquish]], to [[defeat]]
# to [[overcome]]
# to [[beat]]

====Usage notes====
* In the first-person singular, the phrase "{{m|ru|[[одержа́ть]] [[побе́ду]]}}" is used instead.

====Conjugation====
{{ru-conj|pf|4b+pжд|победи́ть|futr_1sg=-}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ru|побе́да}}
* {{l|ru|победи́тель}}
* {{l|ru|побе́дный}}
* {{l|ru|победоно́сный}}
